# You design and build LEGO Technic models one step at a time, in a build language.
#
# For each step you write:
# ADD name partnumber color
# CONNECT part.point -> part.point LOCKED|TURNS|STIFF   (points: hole1.., axlehole1.., pin1.., axle1.., clip1..; LOCKED = cross in cross, turn together; TURNS = free; STIFF = friction pin)
# Optional: MESH a.teeth b.teeth / RATIO a b x/y / GROUP g (opens a side build) / END (closes it) / ATTACH g (joins a finished side build into the main model)
# WHY one plain sentence: what this step builds and what it is for.
# A point ending in ~ is an estimate; ? means not known.
#
# Rules: only use real points of each part; a round pin never goes in a cross hole; a shaft that must turn needs round holes; a worm needs stops on both sides; gears must sit at the right distance.
STEP 1
ADD rax-conn1 32013 black
ADD rax-axle1 32073 lightgray
CONNECT rax-axle1.axle3~ -> rax-conn1.axlehole1 LOCKED
WHY Locks a black angled connector to the middle of a long axle to start the rear suspension cross.

STEP 2
ADD rax-arm1 32056 red
ADD rax-arm2 32056 red
CONNECT rax-arm1.axlehole1~ -> rax-axle1.axle1 LOCKED
CONNECT rax-arm2.axlehole1~ -> rax-axle1.axle5 LOCKED
WHY Locks a red L-shaped arm onto each end of the axle so the rear cross can carry the body on both sides.

STEP 3
ADD rax-axle2 3705 black
ADD rax-liftarm1 32192 black
ADD rax-knuckle1 32184 lightgray
CONNECT rax-axle2.axle2~ -> rax-liftarm1.axlehole1 LOCKED
CONNECT rax-axle2.axle3~ -> rax-knuckle1.axlehole1~ LOCKED
WHY Adds a second short axle with a bent liftarm and a double connector to build up the rear block.

STEP 4
ADD rax-liftarm2 32192 black
CONNECT rax-axle2.axle1~ -> rax-liftarm2.axlehole1 LOCKED
WHY Mirrors the bent liftarm onto the other end of the short axle to square up the block.

STEP 5
ADD eng-beam1 60483 white
ADD eng-conn1 32013 black
ADD eng-hub1 15100 darkgray
ADD eng-pin1 11214 red
ADD eng-hub2 87082 red
ADD eng-bush1 32123b lightgray
CONNECT eng-pin1.pin1 -> eng-beam1.hole1~ STIFF
CONNECT eng-hub1.pin1 -> rax-knuckle1.hole1~ STIFF
CONNECT eng-hub2.pin1~ -> eng-conn1.hole1 STIFF
CONNECT eng-bush1.axlehole1~ -> rax-axle2.axle4~ LOCKED
WHY Builds the small engine-block-looking cluster of hubs and a friction pin that will carry the rear drive.

STEP 6
ADD fw-liftarm1 32192 black
CONNECT fw-liftarm1.hole1~ -> eng-pin1.pin2 STIFF
WHY Adds the third bent liftarm, pinned on, to extend the cluster toward the chassis spine.

STEP 7
ADD eng-knuckle2 32184 lightgray
CONNECT eng-knuckle2.hole1~ -> eng-hub2.pin2~ STIFF
WHY Adds the second double connector so the cluster has a free hole ready for the next axle.

STEP 8
ADD ch-axle1 4519 yellow
ADD rax-axle3 32073 lightgray
ADD ch-bentbeam1 32348 black
CONNECT ch-axle1.axle2~ -> eng-knuckle2.axlehole1~ LOCKED
CONNECT rax-axle3.axle3~ -> ch-bentbeam1.axlehole1~ LOCKED
WHY Adds a yellow axle and a long bent beam so the cluster can reach forward into the main chassis.

STEP 9
ADD ch-axle2 4519 yellow
ADD ch-conn1 32039 red
ADD ch-beam1 60483 white
CONNECT ch-axle2.axle1~ -> ch-conn1.axlehole1 LOCKED
CONNECT ch-axle2.axle3~ -> ch-beam1.axlehole1 LOCKED
WHY Builds a short post with a red axle connector that will carry the upright gearbox post.

STEP 10
ADD ch-spine1 32140 black
ADD ch-spine2 32140 black
WHY Adds the first pair of L-shaped thick beams that form the main chassis spine.

STEP 11
ADD ch-spine3 32140 black
ADD ch-spine4 32140 black
WHY Lengthens the chassis spine on both sides with a second pair of L-shaped beams.

STEP 12
ADD ch-brace1 6632 black
ADD ch-brace2 6632 black
ADD ch-brace3 6632 black
ADD ch-brace4 6632 black
WHY Adds four short thin beams that will tie the two sides of the chassis spine together.

STEP 13
ADD ch-thin1 41677 black
ADD ch-thin2 41677 black
ADD ch-stud1 2825 black
ADD ch-stud2 2825 black
ADD ch-stud3 2825 black
CONNECT ch-axle1.axle3~ -> ch-thin1.axlehole1~ LOCKED
CONNECT rax-axle3.axle1~ -> ch-thin2.axlehole1~ LOCKED
WHY Adds short thin beams and stud-connector beams that will later hold the steering column and seat.

STEP 14
ADD pin1 2780 black
ADD pin2 2780 black
ADD pin3 2780 black
ADD pin4 2780 black
ADD pin5 2780 black
CONNECT pin1.pin1 -> ch-brace1.hole1~ STIFF
CONNECT pin1.pin2 -> ch-spine3.hole1~ STIFF
CONNECT pin2.pin1 -> ch-brace2.hole1~ STIFF
CONNECT pin2.pin2 -> ch-spine4.hole1~ STIFF
CONNECT pin3.pin1 -> ch-brace3.hole1~ STIFF
CONNECT pin3.pin2 -> ch-spine1.hole1~ STIFF
CONNECT pin4.pin1 -> ch-brace4.hole1~ STIFF
CONNECT pin4.pin2 -> ch-spine2.hole1~ STIFF
CONNECT pin5.pin1 -> ch-stud1.hole1~ STIFF
CONNECT pin5.pin2 -> ch-spine1.hole2~ STIFF
WHY Pins the four cross braces onto the spine on each side and starts pinning on the stud-connector beam.

STEP 15
ADD pin6 2780 black
ADD pin7 2780 black
ADD pin8 2780 black
ADD pin9 2780 black
ADD pin10 2780 black
ADD link1 3673 lightgray
ADD link2 3673 lightgray
CONNECT pin6.pin1 -> ch-stud2.hole1~ STIFF
CONNECT pin6.pin2 -> ch-spine2.hole2~ STIFF
CONNECT pin7.pin1 -> ch-stud3.hole1~ STIFF
CONNECT pin7.pin2 -> ch-spine3.hole2~ STIFF
CONNECT pin8.pin1 -> ch-bentbeam1.hole1~ STIFF
CONNECT pin8.pin2 -> ch-spine1.hole3~ STIFF
CONNECT pin9.pin1 -> ch-bentbeam1.hole3~ STIFF
CONNECT pin9.pin2 -> ch-spine2.hole3~ STIFF
CONNECT link1.pin1 -> ch-spine3.hole3~ TURNS
CONNECT link2.pin1 -> ch-spine4.hole2~ TURNS
WHY Finishes pinning the spine, ties the long bent beam into it, and adds two frictionless pins where a later part needs to swing freely.

STEP 16
ADD nose-panelA1 11946 brightorange
ADD nose-panelB1 11947 brightorange
ADD nose-beam1 32523 brightorange
CONNECT pin10.pin1 -> nose-beam1.hole2~ STIFF
CONNECT pin10.pin2 -> ch-spine4.hole3~ STIFF
CONNECT ch-axle1.axle1~ -> nose-panelA1.axlehole1~ LOCKED
WHY Starts the front nose shell with the first panel pair and a short orange beam carrying the race number sticker.

STEP 17
ADD nose-panelA2 11946 brightorange
ADD nose-panelB2 11947 brightorange
ADD nose-top1 32316 brightorange
ADD nose-top2 32316 brightorange
CONNECT rax-axle3.axle2~ -> nose-panelB1.axlehole1~ LOCKED
CONNECT rax-axle3.axle4~ -> nose-panelB2.axlehole1~ LOCKED
WHY Mirrors the nose panels on the other side and adds the two orange beams that cap the top of the nose.

STEP 18
ADD nose-base1 32316 black
ADD nose-base2 32316 black
CONNECT ch-axle2.axle2~ -> nose-panelA2.axlehole1~ LOCKED
WHY Adds two black beams under the nose shell to brace the panels from underneath.

STEP 19
ADD sus-knuckle1 92907 black
ADD sus-bush1 3713 red
ADD sus-pin1 3749 tan
ADD whl-wheel1 55982 white
ADD whl-tyre1 92402 black
CONNECT sus-pin1.axle1~ -> sus-knuckle1.axlehole1~ LOCKED
CONNECT sus-bush1.axlehole1~ -> sus-pin1.axle1~ LOCKED
CONNECT sus-pin1.pin1 -> whl-wheel1.hole1 TURNS
DOES sus-pin1 SPINS_ON whl-wheel1
WHY Builds the steering knuckle for the front-left corner and mounts its wheel and tyre.

STEP 20
ADD whl-knuckle2 32291 black
ADD whl-bush2 3713 red
ADD whl-pin2 3749 tan
ADD whl-wheel2 55982 white
ADD whl-tyre2 92402 black
CONNECT whl-pin2.axle1~ -> whl-knuckle2.axlehole1~ LOCKED
CONNECT whl-bush2.axlehole1~ -> whl-pin2.axle1~ LOCKED
CONNECT whl-pin2.pin1 -> whl-wheel2.hole1 TURNS
DOES whl-pin2 SPINS_ON whl-wheel2
WHY Mounts the second wheel corner the same way as the first.

STEP 21
ADD whl-knuckle3 32291 black
ADD whl-bush3 3713 red
ADD whl-pin3 3749 tan
ADD whl-wheel3 55982 white
ADD whl-tyre3 92402 black
CONNECT whl-pin3.axle1~ -> whl-knuckle3.axlehole1~ LOCKED
CONNECT whl-bush3.axlehole1~ -> whl-pin3.axle1~ LOCKED
CONNECT whl-pin3.pin1 -> whl-wheel3.hole1 TURNS
DOES whl-pin3 SPINS_ON whl-wheel3
WHY Mounts the third wheel corner.

STEP 22
ADD whl-knuckle4 32291 black
ADD whl-bush4 3713 red
ADD whl-pin4 3749 tan
ADD whl-wheel4 55982 white
ADD whl-tyre4 92402 black
CONNECT whl-pin4.axle1~ -> whl-knuckle4.axlehole1~ LOCKED
CONNECT whl-bush4.axlehole1~ -> whl-pin4.axle1~ LOCKED
CONNECT whl-pin4.pin1 -> whl-wheel4.hole1 TURNS
DOES whl-pin4 SPINS_ON whl-wheel4
WHY Mounts the fourth and last wheel corner so the buggy stands on all four wheels.

STEP 23
ADD sus-conn1 59443 lightgray
ADD sus-pin5 4274 lightgray
ADD sus-steer1 6553 black
ADD sus-pin6 3749 tan
CONNECT sus-pin6.axle1~ -> sus-conn1.axlehole1~ LOCKED
CONNECT sus-steer1.axle1~ -> sus-conn1.axlehole2~ LOCKED
CONNECT sus-pin5.pin1 -> whl-wheel1.hole1 TURNS
DOES sus-steer1 DRIVES sus-conn1
WHY Adds the steering arm and a smooth connector so the front-left knuckle can be turned from the chassis.

STEP 24
ADD sus-shock1 76138 lightgray
CONNECT ch-axle2.axle2~ -> sus-shock1.hole1~ TURNS
CONNECT sus-pin5.pin2 -> sus-shock1.hole2~ TURNS
WHY Fits the soft spring shock absorber between the chassis and the front-left steering arm to soak up bumps.

STEP 25
ADD ch-axle3 24316 brown
ADD ch-axle4 24316 brown
CONNECT ch-axle3.axle1~ -> ch-brace1.axlehole1~ LOCKED
CONNECT ch-axle4.axle1~ -> ch-brace2.axlehole1~ LOCKED
WHY Adds two stopped axles through the cross braces that hold the rear drive parts from sliding sideways.

STEP 26
ADD ch-axle5 32062 red
ADD ch-axle6 32062 red
ADD ch-axle7 32062 red
ADD ch-axle8 32062 red
CONNECT ch-axle5.axle1~ -> ch-brace3.axlehole1~ LOCKED
CONNECT ch-axle6.axle1~ -> ch-brace4.axlehole1~ LOCKED
CONNECT ch-axle7.axle1~ -> ch-bentbeam1.axlehole2~ LOCKED
CONNECT ch-axle8.axle1~ -> rax-knuckle1.axlehole2~ LOCKED
WHY Adds short notched axles that link the cross braces and knuckle so later parts can turn on them.

STEP 27
ADD ch-axle9 32062 red
ADD ch-axle10 32062 red
ADD ch-axle11 32062 red
ADD fw-tooth1 48267 red
ADD fw-tooth2 48267 red
CONNECT fw-tooth1.axlehole1~ -> ch-axle9.axle1~ LOCKED
CONNECT fw-tooth2.axlehole1~ -> ch-axle10.axle1~ LOCKED
WHY Adds the toothed ratchet parts that will let the pull-cord wind the flywheel one way only.

STEP 28
ADD fw-gear1 32270 black
ADD fw-shaft1 60485 lightgray
CONNECT fw-gear1.axlehole1~ -> fw-shaft1.axle2~ LOCKED
CONNECT fw-shaft1.axle8~ -> eng-knuckle2.axlehole2~ LOCKED
DOES fw-shaft1 DRIVES fw-gear1
WHY Mounts the double-bevel gear on the long shaft that will carry the pull-cord wing.

STEP 29
ADD fw-conn1 6536 black
ADD fw-conn2 42003 black
ADD fw-conn3 42003 black
CONNECT fw-shaft1.axle1~ -> fw-conn1.axlehole1~ LOCKED
CONNECT ch-axle11.axle1~ -> fw-conn2.axlehole1~ LOCKED
CONNECT ch-axle9.axle2~ -> fw-conn3.axlehole1~ LOCKED
WHY Adds the perpendicular connectors that hold the flywheel shaft square to the chassis.

STEP 30
ADD misc-conn1 32039 red
ADD misc-pin1 32002 tan
ADD misc-pin2 43093 blue
ADD misc-pin3 43093 blue
CONNECT fw-shaft1.axle4~ -> misc-conn1.axlehole1~ LOCKED
CONNECT misc-pin1.pin1 -> fw-conn2.hole1~ TURNS
CONNECT misc-pin2.axle1~ -> fw-conn3.axlehole1~ LOCKED
CONNECT misc-pin3.pin1 -> fw-conn1.hole1~ STIFF
WHY Adds a few more friction pins and an axle connector that stiffen the flywheel mount.

STEP 31
ADD side-pin1 6558 blue
ADD side-pin2 6558 blue
CONNECT side-pin1.pin1 -> ch-spine3.hole4~ STIFF
CONNECT side-pin2.pin1 -> ch-spine4.hole4~ STIFF
WHY Adds the two long friction pins that will anchor the side hose tubes.

STEP 32
ADD ch-axle12 4519 yellow
ADD ch-axle13 3705 black
ADD ch-axle14 3705 black
ADD ch-axle15 3705 black
ADD rax-axle4 32073 lightgray
CONNECT ch-axle12.axle1~ -> fw-conn1.axlehole1~ LOCKED
CONNECT ch-axle13.axle1~ -> ch-thin1.axlehole2~ LOCKED
CONNECT ch-axle14.axle1~ -> ch-thin2.axlehole2~ LOCKED
CONNECT ch-axle15.axle1~ -> ch-conn1.axlehole2~ LOCKED
CONNECT rax-axle4.axle1~ -> rax-liftarm1.axlehole2~ LOCKED
WHY Adds the last short axles that finish bracing the rear half of the chassis.

STEP 33
ADD body-bush1 32123b lightgray
ADD body-bush2 32123b lightgray
ADD body-bush3 32123b lightgray
CONNECT ch-axle13.axle2~ -> body-bush1.axlehole1~ LOCKED
CONNECT ch-axle14.axle2~ -> body-bush2.axlehole1~ LOCKED
CONNECT ch-axle15.axle2~ -> body-bush3.axlehole1~ LOCKED
WHY Adds the last three smooth bushes onto the rear axles so they turn freely instead of binding.

STEP 34
ADD side-hose1 75c09 brightorange
ADD side-hose2 75c09 brightorange
CONNECT side-pin1.pin2 -> side-hose1.end1? STIFF
CONNECT side-pin2.pin2 -> side-hose2.end1? STIFF
WHY Fits the two rigid orange hoses that curve from the chassis up to the pull-cord wing.

STEP 35
ADD misc-pin4 11214 red
ADD steer-wheel1 16091 lightgray
CONNECT misc-pin4.pin1 -> fw-conn2.hole2~ STIFF
CONNECT misc-pin4.axle1~ -> steer-wheel1.hole1? LOCKED
WHY Plugs the small steering wheel onto a friction pin on the dashboard connector so the driver has something to hold.

STEP 36
ADD ch-bentbeam2 32348 black
CONNECT ch-bentbeam2.hole1~ -> side-hose1.end2? STIFF
CONNECT ch-bentbeam2.hole3~ -> side-hose2.end2? STIFF
WHY Fits the last bent beam across the tops of the two hoses, bracing the pull-cord wing and completing the buggy.
